{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026","id":1351250,"title":"Toys in Creation\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-27T03:31:54-08:00","id":1351250,"title":"Toys in Creation\u2026","content":"One of my players asked me about the availability/prevalence of teddy bears in Chiaroscuro, and after a dive into Wikipedia on the history of stuffed animals (I decided I wouldn\u2019t rule them out entirely, but dolls would be far more common), it occurred to me to be curious about other toys.<br /> <br /> What sort of stuff do your kids play with, in your Creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T04:26:59-08:00","id":1351253,"title":"","content":"Humans have apparently been putting wheels on animals for millennia, so that could be a thing.<br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/a3/5f/00/a35f005d66b610a4b9e7b63017ae24f4.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T04:45:18-08:00","id":1351256,"title":"","content":"I can't help but imagine mortal toys as having a horror slant to them, what with mortals being surrounded by deadly danger on all sides. I could see children playing with small figurines of hungry dead and fleeing humans. Dolls which are given to children telling them Lunar Ogres make them by putting the souls of bad children in them. Stink bombs vaunted as being made from &quot;real blood ape breath&quot;. That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T04:51:04-08:00","id":1351259,"title":"","content":"Spinning tops. Toy soldiers. Various animals, both natural and unnatural.<br /> Lots of different ball games, especially the Aztec one in some parts of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:10:29-08:00","id":1351280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026#post1351250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What sort of stuff do your kids play with, in your Creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the emphasis on artisan crafts in Whitewall, in addition to moveable type, there are Syndic figurines that go along with childrens books that tell simple allegories concerning the Syndics, that ties into a particular aspect of the Whitewall charter and pages of basic laws that all children have to memorize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:44:53-08:00","id":1351284,"title":"","content":"Honestly, teddies are one I'd personally avoid, given their cultural links to a real world figure/historical point. I'm more inclined to run with carved figures, with maybe soft woven dolls for the young or those in need of comfort. More specifics and form are going to be locally dependent - I could see the Guild sponsoring dolls of the Hierarchs to try and give themselves a bit of an image boost for giving toys to children, whereas in the Realm kids may get either abstract dragon toys, or ones with a militirstic slant (Gateway sets being the prime example.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4086-croakamancer","name":"Croakamancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4086_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:27:55-08:00","id":1351312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351259#post1351259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lots of different ball games, especially the Aztec one in some parts of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why especially that one? Jeez, there's been more than one ball game prior to the 19th century.<br /> <br /> I'd say various kinds of whistle can serve as a toy and rudimentary instrument. Perhaps a few other kinds of noisemaker.<br /> <br /> I wonder what would be needed for little mechanical catapults, although those are likely on the more expensive side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:52:27-08:00","id":1351319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351256#post1351256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but imagine mortal toys as having a horror slant to them, what with mortals being surrounded by deadly danger on all sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this might be an overly-grim take on it. I'd compare it to real-world practices from Earth. In the real world, before the modern day and outside the rich First World economies, the average person was often surrounded by deadly danger, to much the same degree that someone in Creation is. Plague, war, abusive authority figures, and so forth all existed. But most cultures didn't develop toys that involved them. Rather, I'd expect that most toys in Creation follow similar patterns to those on Earth, being some combination of representations of domestic people and objects (things like dolls that represent average people or common farm animals and miniature versions of common tools or vehicles), representations of heroic or aspirational figures (dolls that represent standard iconography of heroic or legendary figures, toy soldiers, toy weapons, and so on), and objects that combine ease of creation and teaching basic life skills like hand-eye coordination (balls, sticks, jacks, etc.). <br /> <br /> I think in areas where the Immaculate Faith is dominant, you'd be less likely to see dolls, particularly of the &quot;aspirational&quot; or &quot;heroic&quot; type. That's due to both the Immaculates' aniconic stance, and because I think it would go against general Immaculate doctrine that people shouldn't try to rise above their station. An Immaculate monk who saw a child playing with a doll that looked like a Dragon-Blood and pretending to be such a person would probably deliver a lecture, if not a more severe response. <br /> <br /> Outside of Immaculate-controlled areas, dolls that represent Dragon-Blooded would be much more common, I'd think. Even in Lunar Dominions, unless the Lunar was particularly set against Dragon-Blooded in general rather than the Realm in particular, the Dragon-Blooded are probably the most visible and obvious heroic figures in most of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T12:37:31-08:00","id":1351343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Croakamancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351284#post1351284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, teddies are one I'd personally avoid, given their cultural links to a real world figure/historical point.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">You mean Rider in the Roughs, the Lunar who seized power by the twin strategies of populist rhetoric and dangerously adorable stuffed toys?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T15:36:42-08:00","id":1351371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351319#post1351319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this might be an overly-grim take on it. I'd compare it to real-world practices from Earth. In the real world, before the modern day and outside the rich First World economies, the average person was often surrounded by deadly danger, to much the same degree that someone in Creation is. Plague, war, abusive authority figures, and so forth all existed. But most cultures didn't develop toys that involved them. Rather, I'd expect that most toys in Creation follow similar patterns to those on Earth, being some combination of representations of domestic people and objects (things like dolls that represent average people or common farm animals and miniature versions of common tools or vehicles), representations of heroic or aspirational figures (dolls that represent standard iconography of heroic or legendary figures, toy soldiers, toy weapons, and so on), and objects that combine ease of creation and teaching basic life skills like hand-eye coordination (balls, sticks, jacks, etc.).<br /> <br /> I think in areas where the Immaculate Faith is dominant, you'd be less likely to see dolls, particularly of the &quot;aspirational&quot; or &quot;heroic&quot; type. That's due to both the Immaculates' aniconic stance, and because I think it would go against general Immaculate doctrine that people shouldn't try to rise above their station. An Immaculate monk who saw a child playing with a doll that looked like a Dragon-Blood and pretending to be such a person would probably deliver a lecture, if not a more severe response.<br /> <br /> Outside of Immaculate-controlled areas, dolls that represent Dragon-Blooded would be much more common, I'd think. Even in Lunar Dominions, unless the Lunar was particularly set against Dragon-Blooded in general rather than the Realm in particular, the Dragon-Blooded are probably the most visible and obvious heroic figures in most of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Immaculate Faith, as in the religion of the Shogunate, is not aniconic, if Lookshy is any indication. The Immaculate Order is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T15:53:22-08:00","id":1351373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351312#post1351312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why especially that one? Jeez, there's been more than one ball game prior to the 19th century.<br /> <br /> I'd say various kinds of whistle can serve as a toy and rudimentary instrument. Perhaps a few other kinds of noisemaker.<br /> <br /> I wonder what would be needed for little mechanical catapults, although those are likely on the more expensive side.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=8pF03BXxUSY\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=8pF03BXxUSY</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T20:03:58-08:00","id":1351402,"title":"","content":"First off, I love this question. Its so good. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351259#post1351259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spinning tops. Toy soldiers. Various animals, both natural and unnatural.<br /> Lots of different ball games</div> </div> </div> </div>Toy soldiers 100%. Hubters and priests and other easily recognizable jobs too. Thats has shown up in many, many world cultures. Animals even more so. <br /> <br /> Dolls are everywhere, but pay attention to materials. Cotton might be rare in some places, so wood or leather is more common dolls are usually made from left overs. I remember reading that Puritans favored cloth dolls because they didnt make noise when dropped in church (possibly apocryphal). little Things like that go a long way. <br /> <br /> A little boy on the Blessed Isle probably has fills dressed like dynast troops. Give them some life. <br /> <br /> On the subject of ball games, i make reference to every place having their own version of the basic &quot;take this ball to that area and you score&quot;, which encompasses Soccer, Am Football, Rugby, Basketball, Aussie Football, Lacrosse, Hockey, Polo, and everything besides baseball that isnt a martial sport.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:07:51-08:00","id":1351470,"title":"","content":"It's mentioned in the Realm that people there play Cujo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:11:23-08:00","id":1351473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351250-toys-in-creation\u2026?p=1351470#post1351470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's mentioned in the Realm that people there play Cujo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cujo?<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm unfamiliar with it, unless you're referring to people in Creation playing horrific games with rabid Saint Bernard dogs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-28-2019, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T07:16:20-08:00","id":1351474,"title":"","content":"<d